We had a fan question from Brittany Y., Sarah M., and many more.

808
00:28:09.240 --> 00:28:11.840
Who is the baby that played Astrid?

809
00:28:12.140 --> 00:28:13.360
I will tell you.

810
00:28:13.500 --> 00:28:14.760
Thanks to Jamesopedia.

811
00:28:15.420 --> 00:28:19.460
First of all, you know, babies are played by many babies.

812
00:28:20.560 --> 00:28:22.120
Sometimes they're a set of twins.

813
00:28:22.120 --> 00:28:25.380
Like in the case of Cece, Cece was this set of twins,

814
00:28:25.940 --> 00:28:29.200
and it was the same twin girls all through the show.

815
00:28:29.400 --> 00:28:31.920
They were absolute sweethearts, and I loved them.

816
00:28:31.920 --> 00:28:38.800
But sometimes, especially with a baby this little, it's like three babies, five babies, lots of babies.

817
00:28:38.940 --> 00:28:42.340
Oh, Philip was several different babies and then a different toddler.

818
00:28:42.920 --> 00:28:43.320
Yes.

819
00:28:43.660 --> 00:28:47.560
So this is because there are rules about babies working on a set.

820
00:28:47.680 --> 00:28:49.860
They can only work for like 20 minutes.

821
00:28:50.140 --> 00:28:51.480
And I think that's a good thing.

822
00:28:51.700 --> 00:28:52.100
Yes.

823
00:28:53.020 --> 00:28:58.080
Also, if you have a baby and one of them's fussy, you can swap them out for a different baby.

824
00:28:58.080 --> 00:28:59.260
They're all dressed the same.

825
00:28:59.420 --> 00:29:01.940
You go backstage and there's like six babies in the same outfit.

826
00:29:02.340 --> 00:29:07.880
So Astrid was played first by a set of twins and another baby.

827
00:29:08.120 --> 00:29:09.420
Here's the crazy thing.

828
00:29:09.740 --> 00:29:12.940
The twins' names were Matthew and Joey Levinson.

829
00:29:13.500 --> 00:29:14.120
Crazy.

830
00:29:14.420 --> 00:29:14.720
Right?

831
00:29:14.820 --> 00:29:17.080
And they were playing Jan Levinson's baby.

832
00:29:17.220 --> 00:29:17.620
Yes.

833
00:29:17.860 --> 00:29:20.160
The other baby was Harvey Green.

834
00:29:20.380 --> 00:29:23.600
So her babies were the Levinson Green babies.

835
00:29:23.600 --> 00:29:24.080
Okay.

836
00:29:25.120 --> 00:29:25.760
All right.

837
00:29:25.940 --> 00:29:27.260
And then that was on one day.

838
00:29:27.480 --> 00:29:31.560
The other day, we had a set of triplets playing Astrid.

839
00:29:31.900 --> 00:29:34.800
They were Chase, Chloe, and Juliet Purcell.

840
00:29:35.140 --> 00:29:37.040
So those are all the babies.

841
00:29:37.160 --> 00:29:38.340
We also had a fake baby.

842
00:29:38.540 --> 00:29:40.000
We did have a fake baby.

843
00:29:40.100 --> 00:29:40.240
Yeah.

844
00:29:40.240 --> 00:29:47.620
And it's really funny because if you look at the call sheet, scene by scene, it'll say real baby or fake baby.

845
00:29:48.020 --> 00:29:49.580
Like what we're using in the scene.

846
00:29:49.720 --> 00:29:51.000
And they would stagger them, right?

847
00:29:51.100 --> 00:29:52.920
Because the babies could only work for 20 minutes.

848
00:29:53.340 --> 00:29:56.840
So you'd have a scene with a real baby and then a scene with a fake baby.

849
00:29:56.840 --> 00:30:01.680
Well, Michael walks out of the kitchen and he sees Jan with the baby.

850
00:30:02.020 --> 00:30:03.620
I can't imagine how he felt.

851
00:30:03.820 --> 00:30:06.160
He'd been to all of his birthing classes with her.

852
00:30:06.680 --> 00:30:09.380
And then he was sort of left out of this big moment.

853
00:30:10.000 --> 00:30:11.980
And he confronts Jan about it.

854
00:30:12.240 --> 00:30:14.980
This is one of my favorite couplets of dialogue from the whole episode.

855
00:30:14.980 --> 00:30:15.900
Okay.

856
00:30:16.260 --> 00:30:17.240
It's so rich.

857
00:30:17.480 --> 00:30:19.400
Michael says, why didn't you call me?

858
00:30:19.520 --> 00:30:20.400
I could have helped.

859
00:30:20.820 --> 00:30:24.560
Jan said, well, the birth instructor thought it wasn't a good idea for you to be there.

860
00:30:24.780 --> 00:30:30.680
So Michael says, oh man, him, that guy, he had no sense of humor.

861
00:30:30.820 --> 00:30:33.400
And I proved him wrong in so many ways.

862
00:30:33.820 --> 00:30:36.440
And it just made me think about these classes.

863
00:30:36.680 --> 00:30:42.340
I wish we could have seen Michael trying to do comedy bits with like a birthing instructor.

864
00:30:42.820 --> 00:30:44.620
I would have loved to seen that scene.

865
00:30:44.980 --> 00:30:47.880
I think what Jan has done to Michael is so cruel.

866
00:30:47.940 --> 00:30:50.680
I know that she didn't call him.

867
00:30:50.840 --> 00:30:55.260
And also in that scene, Jan is like, Michael, you don't know what I've been through.

868
00:30:55.420 --> 00:30:57.560
And he said, no, no, I don't.

869
00:30:57.880 --> 00:31:00.080
And I love Steve's delivery on that.

870
00:31:00.200 --> 00:31:00.600
I know.

871
00:31:00.880 --> 00:31:05.400
I guess she feels bad and she lets him hold the baby, but it says the baby has to stay in the car seat.

872
00:31:05.760 --> 00:31:12.920
And then Michael has this very sweet talking head where he says he loves babies and he tries to pick them up and hold one every day.

873
00:31:13.060 --> 00:31:14.520
It just nourishes him.

874
00:31:15.020 --> 00:31:20.080
And then we see this really sweet montage of Michael and babies and the babies love him.

875
00:31:20.220 --> 00:31:21.080
They really do.

876
00:31:21.420 --> 00:31:24.820
Well, that's because it's Steve Carell is holding the baby.

877
00:31:25.060 --> 00:31:25.180
I know.

878
00:31:25.280 --> 00:31:29.540
I mean, not to say that they wouldn't have loved Michael, but Steve is a natural with kids.

879
00:31:29.700 --> 00:31:30.100
I know.

880
00:31:30.300 --> 00:31:32.400
We had a fan question from Evan L.

881
00:31:32.520 --> 00:31:33.500
and Stacey M.

882
00:31:33.800 --> 00:31:42.560
In the scenes where Michael is holding all the babies, were those hired actors or did the crew just go out and let people line up to have their baby held by Steve Carell?

883
00:31:43.580 --> 00:31:48.740
All of those babies were the children of our writers and our crew.

884
00:31:49.100 --> 00:31:50.960
So here is a list of the babies.

885
00:31:51.240 --> 00:31:54.260
At nine minutes, you have baby on the street.

886
00:31:54.800 --> 00:31:59.040
This is Emma Holland, daughter of our editor, Dean Holland.

887
00:31:59.480 --> 00:32:01.980
And that is also Dean's wife, Tasha.

888
00:32:02.400 --> 00:32:06.760
At nine minutes, nine seconds, I'm calling this one baby at the bathroom.

889
00:32:07.800 --> 00:32:09.960
That baby is Theodore Grandy.

890
00:32:10.200 --> 00:32:12.220
The woman is Sage Grandy.

891
00:32:12.480 --> 00:32:15.460
And this is the son of our writer, Charlie Grandy.

892
00:32:17.020 --> 00:32:20.620
At nine minutes, 15 seconds, we have double baby.

893
00:32:21.040 --> 00:32:23.780
And that is our writer, Mike Schur's wife, J.J.

894
00:32:23.960 --> 00:32:30.540
Philbin, and their baby, William, along with our camera operator, Matt Soane's wife, Melissa, and their baby, Devin.

895
00:32:31.200 --> 00:32:38.900
And the final baby at nine minutes, 17 seconds, that is Avery Farrell, the daughter of our writer, Anthony Farrell.

896
00:32:39.060 --> 00:32:43.420
The woman was a background performer, but that's Anthony loading the stroller into the car.

897
00:32:43.860 --> 00:32:48.800
So we had had kind of like a little mini baby boom on our set.

898
00:32:49.000 --> 00:32:51.460
All of these kids were around the same age.

899
00:32:51.640 --> 00:32:52.660
I texted with Dean.

900
00:32:52.660 --> 00:33:01.340
He said his daughter, Emma, is now 13 years old, and she tells everybody that she's one of the babies on the office.

901
00:33:01.720 --> 00:33:07.360
And Angela, I know you get asked a lot about Isabel, because she was right around the same age, too.

902
00:33:07.800 --> 00:33:08.180
Yes.

903
00:33:08.360 --> 00:33:09.880
Isabel just had her 13th birthday.

